-3.1 For a local positively oriented future tetrad section $E$ on $U$, define $\Psi_E:U\times SO^+(1,3)\to(P^+_g(M))|_U$ by $\Psi_E(p,A)=E(p)\circ A$. Step 2.1 makes this map bijective. Its inverse sends a frame $u$ over $p$ to $(p,E(p)^{-1}\circ u)$; the matrix entries of this second component are smooth because they are obtained by applying the smooth dual coframe of $E$ to the smooth frame vectors of $u$. Thus $\Psi_E$ is a smooth local product chart. [step 1.1, step 2.1, F4, algebra]
