-4.1 If $E'$ is another such section on an overlap, write $E'(p)=E(p)\circ A(p)$. The coefficients of $A(p)$ are smooth by the same dual-coframe calculation in step 3.1, and step 2.1 places every value in $SO^+(1,3)$. The transition between the charts is $(p,B)\mapsto(p,A(p)B)$, which is smooth; its inverse $(p,B)\mapsto(p,A(p)^{-1}B)$ is smooth because inversion is smooth in the Lie group of [F4]. The right action is smooth in these charts and the projection is the product projection. [step 2.1, step 3.1, F4, algebra]
