-5.1 The charts of step 3.1 and smooth transitions from step 4.1 give $P^+_g(M)$ local products $U\times SO^+(1,3)$. Different base points separate by the Hausdorff base [F6], and distinct frames over one point separate in the Hausdorff matrix group [F4], so the total space is Hausdorff. For second countability, let $\mathcal B$ be a countable base of $M$; for each $B\in\mathcal B$ contained in at least one local-section neighborhood, use [A1] to select one such neighborhood. The selected countable family covers $M$, and countable bases of each selected $U\times SO^+(1,3)$ give a countable base of the total space by [F4,F6]. Thus the local charts define a smooth manifold structure. Freeness and fiberwise transitivity were proved in step 2.1; by [F5], this is a smooth right principal $SO^+(1,3)$-bundle. The construction supplies local sections only, so no global tetrad is asserted. [A1, step 2.1, step 3.1, step 4.1, F4, F5, F6] ∎
